@title Lesson walk: cooling-advice (sweep, headline, options, add, check)
@area Learn
# The lesson from the palette, in the hot cabinet sample. Do it for me only carries out commands, so the Cooling advice button and the Add button are really clicked. The sweep takes about a minute on a worker thread. The window opens in the Cabinet, over the plate.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text cooling advice
wait 6
click_text "Where a vent and fan should go: cooling advice"
wait 40
shot 01-why
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 02-open-cabinet
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 03-heat-on
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 04-press
check_layout
click_text "Cooling advice" Button
wait_s 120
expect "Tightest margin"
expect "Model estimate"
shot 05-sweep-done
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 06-headline
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 07-options
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 08-add
check_layout
click_text "Add these two to Vents and fans"
wait 20
shot 09-added
check_layout
